  "notes": "TIME OF DAY:\n{明|あ}け{方|がた} refers specifically to the period just before sunrise when the sky begins to lighten, typically between 4:00-6:00 AM depending on the season.\n\nRELATED TIME WORDS:\n- {夜明|よあ}け (dawn, daybreak - similar meaning)\n- {日|ひ}の{出|で} (sunrise - the moment the sun appears)\n- {早朝|そうちょう} (early morning)\n- {朝方|あさがた} (toward morning)\n\nFORMS:\n{明|あ}ける (to dawn) + {方|がた} (time period suffix) → the time when it dawns",
